@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>Privacy</PageTitle>

<div class="settings-shell">
    <section class="card-surface settings-card">
        <p class="section-label">Privacy</p>
        <h1>Data handling</h1>
        <p class="panel-copy">
            Habitica credentials stay in this browser unless they are needed to verify your party membership with Habitica. Exports and private device sync do not include your API token.
        </p>

        <div class="settings-grid">
            <MudPaper Class="card-surface action-card" Elevation="0">
                <h2>If the app looks out of date</h2>
                <p>Clear this site's browser data and refresh once. This removes old browser files from earlier deployments.</p>
            </MudPaper>

            <MudPaper Class="card-surface action-card" Elevation="0">
                <h2>Habitica credentials</h2>
                <p>Credentials are used to load your Habitica data and protect private device sync. They are not included in exports. Party sync verifies membership before reading or writing shared party CRON data.</p>
            </MudPaper>

            <MudPaper Class="card-surface action-card" Elevation="0">
                <h2>Local and exported data</h2>
                <p>Saved Habitica data, party history, app messages, gear information, and equipment presets are stored in browser storage. Downloaded backup files are readable, so keep them private.</p>
            </MudPaper>

            <MudPaper Class="card-surface action-card" Elevation="0">
                <h2>Private sync</h2>
                <p>Private device sync stores encrypted data. Shared party sync stores party CRON history and derived party state after membership verification. Hosting providers may process request details such as IP address and timestamps for security.</p>
            </MudPaper>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>
